---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LandingSignal from "../components/LandingSignal.astro";
---

<BaseLayout description="Compare counters, sets, registers, and maps. Use illustrated essays and deterministic labs to see which causal machinery each replicated data structure needs.">
  <LandingSignal />

  <div class="landing-reading">
    <section aria-labelledby="structure-title">
      <h2 id="structure-title">Learn the behavior before the bookkeeping</h2>
      <p>
        A counter, set, register, and map each makes a different promise when
        updates are delivered late or in a different order. Start with that promise.
        Then open the metadata that makes it possible.
      </p>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Counters</dt>
          <dd>Independent increments can combine because addition does not need a winner.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Sets</dt>
          <dd>Removal needs a rule for additions that were observed, concurrent, or replayed later.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Registers</dt>
          <dd>Concurrent writes force a choice: select one value or preserve every sibling.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Maps</dt>
          <dd>Each key composes one of those conflict rules into a larger state model.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="trail-title">
      <h2 id="trail-title">Go deeper when a merge rule raises a question</h2>
      <p>
        The reference atlas connects structures to dots, histories, orders,
        and clocks. Each sheet includes an article and a deterministic lab.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="read-title">
      <h2 id="read-title">Open the machinery when you need it</h2>
      <p>
        When a structure keeps a concurrent value or rejects a stale replay,
        inspect the dots, causal context, and clocks behind that result. The
        mechanism is attached to a concrete question instead of presented as
        vocabulary to memorize first.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use the browser labs to delay messages, make concurrent updates, and
        inspect the replica state behind the merge result.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .landing-reading {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  dl {
    margin-block: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (width < 48rem) {
    :global(.site-main:has(> .landing-signal)) {
      padding-block-start: var(--space-4);
    }

    dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-1);
    }
  }
</style>
